  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>The town of Menton has set up fenced, secure parks reserved for dogs, with a water point, so they can socialise, play and run freely.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>According to the "Installations pour les propriétaires de chiens" page on menton.fr, two parks are dedicated to dogs: at <strong>10 avenue Blasco Ibanez</strong> (Garavan area, below the Parc du Pian) and at <strong>115 corniche Serres de la Madone</strong>. The latter, opened in June 2023, covers about 700 m², is fully fenced, freely open 24/7, with a waste-bag dispenser, bins and a fountain. A third park, opened in November 2023 at the main entrance of the Parc du Pian, is reserved for small dogs (under 10 kg): 220 m², winter hours 8am-6pm, summer hours 8am-8pm. Remember to pick up waste.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: Menton also reserves three beaches for dogs and their owners (Gorbio, Casino, Hawaï in Garavan), according to the town hall — a way to combine a walk and a swim.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Parc du Pian and the Garavan area, at the Italian border, offer lovely complementary walks.</p>
    </div>

